claimed: chunks-size-one — the operator asked why Source is not simply replaced by Chunks (the array-native representation, already measured 5.7x ahead of ZIO's own chunk-native default). Hypothesis: Chunks at size=1 degrades the same way ZStream(chunkSize=1) measured 12x worse than okay's per-element Source -- an array-of-chunks representation pays a chunk allocation per production regardless of size, which is exactly the pathology found in ZIO. If true, collapsing Source into Chunks would make a genuinely one-at-a-time live source (LLM tokens, SSE) as slow as ZIO's own worst case, which is the actual reason the two types stay separate rather than an unexamined assumption. Measure Chunks.merge at size=1 against Source.merge on the same elements.
